WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.160
Welcome to the Study Room Reservation
System for Prairie View A&M.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.222
In the next few minutes, we'll show
you how to find and book a study room,

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:12.625
how to manage your bookings, and
how staff keep rooms running.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.420
Then we'll show how our team built it.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.340
To get started, choose Create account.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.410
Enter your name, your student ID,
and your email, and pick a password.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.990
We email you a six-digit code to confirm it's you.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.250
After that, you just log in
with your email and password.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.700
Choose Find a room.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.460
Filter by group size, by features like a
whiteboard or a screen, and by the time you need.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.490
You'll only see rooms that are
open and big enough for your group.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.600
Open a room to see its whole day at a glance.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.690
Open half-hours are green.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:56.190
Booked and closed times are marked, so you
never pick a time that's already taken.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.810
Pick a start time and how long
you need, up to three hours.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.580
Add your group size, and choose Reserve.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:09.500
Your booking is confirmed right away, and you can
add it to Outlook or any calendar with one click.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.010
Your bookings live on your dashboard.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.520
You can change the time or cancel.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.870
When you cancel, the room opens
up for other students right away.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.580
If staff ever need your room,
you're not left stranded.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:30.300
You get an email and a notice here, with another
room or time the system has already found for you.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.960
Choose Move me, and you're rebooked.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.100
Need help?

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.850
The assistant button is on every page.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:43.420
Ask in plain words, like: find me a
room for four people tomorrow at two.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.410
It answers using live availability.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:52.180
At the top of every page, you can
turn on larger text or high contrast.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.780
Your choice is saved to your account.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.080
Staff sign in to the admin center.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:05.110
A short daily brief sums up the day: how busy rooms
are, what was turned away, and what needs attention.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:11.510
Below it, staff see every booking, each room's
status, and booking attempts the system refused.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:17.190
To close a room for an event or
repairs, staff block the time.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:22.450
Anyone booked in that window is notified
and offered another room automatically.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:27.290
Analytics shows usage by day, by hour, and by room.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.050
Every chart has a table view, so
it works with screen readers too.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.780
Here's how we got here.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.629
In Sprint 1, our team built a
React front end on sample data,

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:44.161
a Supabase Postgres database,
and a Node and Express API.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.850
The most important rule, no double bookings,
is enforced by the database itself.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:54.690
Alex books Study Room 106 from 2 to 4 PM.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:58.740
When Jordan tries 3 to 5 PM, Postgres refuses it.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.890
4 to 5 PM is fine, because
back-to-back bookings don't overlap.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:07.250
The three-hour limit and room
capacity are checked the same way.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:12.760
The Express API turns those
database errors into clear answers.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.890
A conflict becomes a 409 error with the code
ROOM_TAKEN, which the app shows in plain words.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.785
In Sprint 2, we moved to Base44 to put
a live, public app in front of users,

00:03:24.785 --> 00:03:30.174
carrying the same rules over and testing
them automatically on every pull request.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.630
Over the following sprints we
added staff tools, calendar export,

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:39.762
the AI assistant, and the rebooking and
accessibility features you just saw.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.770
That's the Study Room Reservation System.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.130
Try it at the address on screen.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.140
Thanks for watching.
